Step 2: Demonstrating Schema Flexibility Insert two completely different products into the
same catalog collection without executing a CREATE TABLE command:

JavaScript
// Insert a laptop (electronics)
db.catalog.insertOne({
product_id: 101,
name: &quot;ThinkPad T14&quot;,
category: &quot;Electronics&quot;,
specs: {
ram: &quot;16GB&quot;,
cpu: &quot;i7&quot;
},
price: 1200.00
});
// Insert a coffee mug (home goods) into the EXACT SAME collection
db.catalog.insertOne({
product_id: 102,
name: &quot;Ceramic Travel Mug&quot;,
category: &quot;Home&quot;,
volume_oz: 16,
is_dishwasher_safe: true,
price: 18.50
});
Step 3: Querying the NoSQL Data Use JSON-based query filters instead of standard
SQL SELECT statements to retrieve your data:

JavaScript
// Find all electronics
db.catalog.find({ category: &quot;Electronics&quot; });
// Find products priced over $50 using the $gt (Greater Than) operator
db.catalog.find({ price: { $gt: 50 } });
